{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 62, :comments ["<b>These, and they were not found</b> — Some say: it is joined with their record, for the word is combined from two [words] in the manner of תקראנה מלחמה [i.e., as a construct form joining elements]. And the correct view in my eyes: it is joined with those registered, namely the sons of Jedaiah mentioned above, and they were not found in their genealogical record; therefore they were removed from the priesthood, for the word ויגואלו מן הכהונה is like לחם מגואל, meaning: they were rejected. And some say: the alef is in place of the ayin."], :book :ezra, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Ezra -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:41:41.990926856Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}